WEBVTT

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:41.040
<i>Distant Passion</i>

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:51.180
No doubt the sound has changed.
Previously, it had a much more dry sound.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.490
But it doesn't seem to be broken.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.320
If te bothers you, why don't you dismantle it?

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.000
You've dismantled it yourself before, right?

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.740
Even if I dismantle it, I don't think I'll find anything wrong.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:09.190
It's just that, like it's trying to convey to me,

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:12.470
the way the engine breathes has changed.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.180
I feel that something is lost...

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:20.250
If I just leave it as it is,though I think it won't happen...

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.840
I'm afraid Z itself will change.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.600
You're pretty sentimental.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.230
Men are strange when it comes to that.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.020
No matter how special a feeling you have towards Z,

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.860
it's still a machine. So if something is
wrong, you'll still have to dismantle it, right?

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:45.320
That's true, after all. That's why, I came to see you.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.880
This is Tsukuba Circuit from 7 years ago.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.340
That's Kijima-san?

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.350
He recorded 1 minute and 5 seconds with a boosted-up Supra JZA-80.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.350
It was a pretty good figure.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:03:00.970
Yamamoto, I see you're still holding on to those old car magazines?

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.530
You sure are diligent.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.350
This is an R33. 1 minute and 2 seconds with boosted-up specs.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.890
He really was a fast racer.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.980
But they're all boosted-up, right?

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.470
Yes, that's the beauty of it.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.680
That's right.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.560
The shop, Zero, where Kijima was working at,
promoted themselves with boost-up modifications.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.700
Or you could say that was the only way.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:27.630
Zero gained fame with Tominaga's CPU
and Kijima's Tsukuba Attack.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.920
When Zero tried Rotary Tuning for the firs time,

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.370
Kijima brought along a young tuner called Machida.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:39.890
During that era of FDs, they were bold
and choose the older model, the FC.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.970
That Machida guy was the real deal.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:48.250
Yeah, making a 2-Rotor 13B work beautifully with a C7 turbine,

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.160
hitting 500hp without any trouble at all.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.350
That was Zero's FC3S.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.160
<i>Say, Kijima, what happened to that FC?</i>

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:12.770
<i>With such a level of tuning, it's not like anybody can simply drive it.</i>

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.090
<i>It was a great car.</i>

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.790
<i>So what about it?</i>

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.140
<i>Does he want me to look for it and drive it once again?</i>

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.030
<i>What use is it telling me all this now after so long?</i>

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.310
This is how I always confirm my feelings one by one.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:41.630
Confirm?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:46.070
Yes, confirm. Between me and Z and whether
we can understand each other properly.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:49.670
It really is a special car...

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:53.420
No, I think it's the same for every car.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.450
Even if we're able to drive it well yesterday,

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.550
it may not be able to run as well today.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:59.910
When you can't drive it well, what do you do?

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.890
I turn back and get off at the nearest exit.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.150
In the past, I couldn't do that. I'd keep on driving until the morning.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.150
But now, I understand. When it won't run, it won't run,

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.140
no matter how much we try to force our feelings into it.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:18.620
Are you really alright with that?

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:19.320
About what?

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.320
About me overhauling his car.

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:23.860
Yeah.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:35.500
This is the power curve during its best condition.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.830
And if we place the current set of data on top of it..

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:42.260
It loses 40hp at the peak.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.860
But the power curve is the same,

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:49.500
there are no strange valleys in the graph and the
boost didn't drop with the increase of the engine rev.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:50.730
There's nothing wrong.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.900
In other words, there's no need for it to be overhauled?

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:57.830
While this is my very own recent theory,

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:01.730
I think any loss of power not more
than 10% cannot be felt by our body.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:06.280
If it's 100hp you minus 10, if it's 300hp then minus 30.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.110
Since Z has 600hp,

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:11.160
I think the loss of anything less than 60hp is not a big deal.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.610
Meaning it's fine the way it is now?

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:15.570
If you say it's not fine, then everything is not fine.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.660
But if you say nothing's wrong, then
there really is nothing wrong with it.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.630
So overall it has weakened.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:25.360
That's right. It's not that something definite
is spoiled, but overall is has weakened.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.340
And we can also say that the machine's specification has expired.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:32.560
If it is reassembled with Rikako-chan's
sense, it will regain power in its own way.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.890
But something lost will never come back again.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:39.050
We won't know that until we try!

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.860
We tried, many times.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.810
For special cars to us like Z,

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:49.860
when a sudden power down occurs, the driver, assembler and me, all three of us

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:54.080
will continuously repeat the trial and error cycle many times.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:59.040
But what has been lost never came back.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.320
The heart of the tuned car was lost.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.960
If you're going out for fun at night,
it's got to be a foreign car after all.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.060
BMWs and Mercedes' cannot be missed.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.650
Isn't that rather flashy?

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:20.890
You mean digging too into it? But that is what's important.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:24.190
Be sure to not choose a second-hand Italian or French car.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.090
If you cause a traffic jam because your car stalled,

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:30.960
it'll be an instant "The End" for you and your girlfriend.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.160
Ok, thank you for your work!

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:39.070
Kijima-san. Can you accompany me today as well?

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:41.710
There's someone I really want you to meet.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:42.420
Me?

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:45.600
Yes, something we talked about some time before,

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.680
the driver of the first generation S30Z.

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.670
Reina-cha, did you come today using your R?

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:55.380
Yes.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:57.890
Will you let me drive it?

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:27.800
As expected, your acceleration is proper. How was my R?

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.850
It's well made, but perhaps the under is a bit too powerful.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:34.310
But at this level, it can be compensated with skill.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:38.990
Rather, with a light suspension, we can't
accelerate into a 200km/h class corner...

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.780
What's wrong?

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:45.660
You always praise foreign cars, but you
actually like local cars as well, right?

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.780
Or rather, you like cars.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:55.990
Yo.

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:01.100
It's rare to see both of you together!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.740
No, coincidently, we met at Wangan.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.830
Ah, let me introduce you all. Kijima-san...

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:10.890
this is Akio-kun, the owner of the Z,

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:13.770
and this is the Emperor of Wangan, BlackBird's Shima-san.

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:16.110
I'm Asakura Akio. Nice to meet you.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.650
I'm Shima Tatsuya.

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:19.270
Nice to meet you.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:26.730
<i>These two are now in the struggle for the
top spot of the Shutokou, Z and BlackBird.</i>

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:31.950
It's a bit sudden, but if it's fine with you, could you drive my Z?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:39.960
Please drive it. You don't have to say anything.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.600
We will follow in Reina's R.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.580
It's fine if you leave us behind.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.600
Are you coming along together?

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.090
Yeah.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:02.790
<i>It's stable. 900rpm, the idling is just right...</i>

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.370
Are the corners at Yokohama really so near?!

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:33.960
W-Wait, isn't he being a little too dangerous all of a sudden?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:36.590
It's all right. He's driving properly.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:41.300
<i>He is properly communicating with the car.</i>

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:42.440
5th gear.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:50.240
<i>Amazing! So this is Kitami Jun's Z...</i>

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:53.570
<i>Is it really so great?! Machida!</i>

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:15.030
Fast!

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:17.260
As expected, seems like he's gotten used to it immediately.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.270
<i>He's starting to drive well.</i>

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:24.980
It's great! Machida, it's great, this thing!

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.840
<i>As a mechanic, I won't known unless
I directly communicate with it properly,</i>

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.340
<i>since Kijima-san is always bluffing.</i>

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:36.200
<i>The torque. The torque is good.</i>

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:39.910
<i>That's right, this car has a nice torque feeling.</i>

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:43.810
<i>This strong feeling of the rising torque
stacking on top of the engine rev.</i>

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:46.220
<i>The strength of the torque itself, which turns the crankshaft.</i>

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:51.000
Machida, why aren't you right here next to me now?

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.450
I won't be able to convey something like this to you!

00:11:55.320 --> 00:12:00.180
Where are you now? What are you
doing now? What happened to that FC?

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:17.270
There was a mechanic who has good sense in our shop,

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:21.710
and he could make even a standard boost-up quite amazing.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.680
I haven't seen him for the past 5 years,

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:27.100
and I don't even know where he is and what is he doing now.

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:30.880
I want to show him this Z.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:35.680
If it's him, I'm sure he will be able to
create something better than this Z.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.770
<i>This is bad, I can't concentrate.</i>

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.970
<i>I can't get it out of my head, that Z.</i>

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:07.530
<i>Damn! I've started to move, now I can't stop anymore.</i>

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:13.210
Then, before we end I'm going to introduce an e-mail.

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:17.590
<i>"I've always enjoyed the show. I have a message for an old racer friend."</i>

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:21.090
Message? Is there such a thing in this show?

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:26.820
<i>"Machida-san who was with the shop Zero,
please contact me. Let's do it once more, Kei."</i>

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.550
Machida-san, could you be watching?

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:31.030
<i>Until next time.</i>

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:32.380
<i>Goodbye.</i>

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:34.500
<i>Drive Go Go.</i>

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:39.280
Hey, hey, are you serious? You never change, bluffing as always.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:48.500
<i>You should just think about the center of gravity of a car.</i>

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.520
<i>Where the center of gravity is right now,</i>

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:56.460
<i>during acceleration, deceleration or cornering,</i>

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:58.510
<i>the center of gravity always changes,</i>

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:00.250
<i>and we should comprehend the meaning of it.</i>

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:03.260
<i>The center of gravity equals to the point of load.</i>

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:08.450
<i>For an RR car, we load the engine behind the rear wheels,</i>

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.250
<i>so that it only drives the rear wheels.</i>

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.230
<i>The rear wheels thus have a heavy load,</i>

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:14.550
<i>and will stay close to the ground.</i>

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:16.720
<i>In other words, it will have good traction.</i>

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:21.230
<i>But if you try to attack seriously at the corner,</i>

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:23.720
<i>with more power the rear wheels will have more traction,</i>

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.230
<i>causing the front wheels to lift.</i>

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:28.450
<i>You can think of it as a see-saw.</i>

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:32.430
<i>Then, we change to 4WDs to prevent that.</i>

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.600
<i>The traction is divided into 4 parts,</i>

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:38.170
<i>preventing all the wheels from lifting
and maintains the grip on the ground.</i>

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:41.670
<i>This is the natural conclusion in the event of pursuing speed.</i>

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:48.510
<i>For the Z, it has an engine with two turbos therefore
the center of gravity is nearer to the front.</i>

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:52.720
<i>Even when you drive it at full speed,
the center of gravity will be around here.</i>

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:55.990
<i>I can't say that there's enough traction.</i>

00:14:56.760 --> 00:15:00.360
<i>Having enough traction means that there is proper load,</i>

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:04.350
<i>which equals us being able to locate the center of gravity.</i>

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:12.700
<i>In its current state, Z cannot go any faster.</i>

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.420
<i>The movement of Z should change according to the way you drive.</i>

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:19.930
<i>Whether Z stays alive or dies, also depends on the driver.</i>

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:21.590
<i>That may be so.</i>

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:24.180
<i>In order for Z to run faster than it does now,</i>

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:30.020
<i>perhaps the only way is to improve my driving skills.</i>

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:38.900
Next up... is the <i>Best 10 Foreign cars chosen by female university students but at ¥2,000,000</i> project.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.950
Oh, isn't that great?

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:47.320
<i>What rubbish. To think that I used to enjoy stuff like this last time.</i>

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:50.320
These are the mails received for the show this week.

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.560
Lately, they've really increased!

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:54.580
Really? Seems like we're getting popular lately.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:57.950
It's good, seriously! It's a waste putting it at midnight.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:00.290
I hope to put this at least around 11pm.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.950
That's great.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:08.670
<i>Boring. After I got involved with that
car, everything about this life is now...</i>

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.560
It's been a while, Kijima-san.

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:27.270
You look fine, Machida.

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:33.490
Papa... hey, papa!

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.820
A 600hp L28 Custom Twin Turbo?

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:37.830
Yeah.

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:42.340
My heart was instantly captured by that Z.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:46.790
Since that happened, there were only two choices left.

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:50.300
Looking away from it and giving up, or...

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:55.770
Whenever I have any spare time,
I always meet up and chat with him.

00:16:55.770 --> 00:17:00.300
About mechanics or driving, petty things and general knowledge.

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:04.780
By talking to him, I realized that there
are many things I've yet to understand.

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:08.660
By telling him these things, I'm returning to being
the person I was from back then once again.

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:20.540
This is my life now.

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:25.580
I've moved away from cars and I'm doing
renovation jobs for mansions and the likes now.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:32.850
Kijima-san, I can understand your feelings,
that you got back your excitement of the past.

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:37.380
In a sense, it's a luxury, since you have money and fame.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:41.680
Kijima-san, you can return if you wanted to,
since you still can fulfill all the conditions for it.

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:44.560
But, I'm different.

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:49.820
This is me now, Kijima-san.

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:58.170
To tell you the truth, I was waiting for you all this time.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:05.120
Even though Zero was disbanded, but one day you'll come for me,

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:08.250
saying, "Machida, let's continue tuning cars again!"

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:12.960
But, five years was a long time.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:17.380
Especially in the tuning world and even for me as well.

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:20.900
I no longer have any intention to go back to that world.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:24.100
Ah, I understand, I'm sorry.

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:28.050
There's no need to apologize! Nothing to apologize about...

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:34.100
Then, goodbye. Take care and be happy.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:37.110
Kijima-san, about that FC...

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.280
This is what you wanted to ask about, right Kijima-san?

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:43.140
Yeah.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:46.050
Please go to Ishikawa Motors in Gotenba.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:47.130
Gotenba?

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:51.100
That Zero's FC was there a year ago.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.630
My investigation ended there.

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:54.690
Machida...

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:57.600
This much was all I could do.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:00.290
Thank you very much. I'm in your debt. That was really helpful.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:01.890
Goodbye.

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:16.650
Feel the road's surface with your palm and
feel the engine with the tip of your toe.

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:21.120
And also feel the G with your back.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:25.580
A car always tries to communicate with the driver.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:37.560
What are you thinking?

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:38.940
Are you free tomorrow?

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:40.940
Yes.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:44.980
Can you come with me, to Gotenba?

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:49.660
There's a car I'm looking for in Gotenba.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.100
That car definitely couldn't have been scrapped.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:53.610
That car?

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:57.570
2nd generation RX-7, FC3S.

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:01.580
For me, this is the only FC that's special.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:07.890
Gotenba Real Estate
For sale

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:08.750
Damn!
Gotenba Real Estate
For sale

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:08.760
Gotenba Real Estate
For sale

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:11.900
No wonder, there's no information about it wherever I called.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:15.410
What should we do? Should we look
for someone who knows about it?

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:20.390
No, we don't have any cars from it.

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:21.660
I see.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:24.870
By Ishikawa Motors, you mean the one near the bypass, huh?

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:27.630
If I'm not mistaken, they closed down half a year ago.

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:30.700
I'm looking for an FC which had been there until last year.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:31.800
FC?

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:35.690
Yes, a 2nd generation RX-7, FC3S.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:38.440
Oh, if it's that car, perhaps...

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:39.910
You know about it?!

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:47.910
It should be around here...

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:50.870
That's the one.

00:20:57.550 --> 00:20:59.880
Excuse me, is anybody there?

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:03.450
Kijima-san, is that...

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:12.770
It's here...

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:17.600
Is it this FC?

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:26.330
Without a doubt, it's this one. It's this FC.

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:29.980
Some minor things like the wheels and mirrors have been changed...

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:35.070
but without a doubt, it's this guy. Why is shining?

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:37.050
It's really is clean.

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:38.750
But it's a bit too clean!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.200
Or more like, it seems strangely firm.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:45.040
When it still was with Zero, it felt much more rickety.

00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:49.010
You guys, you got any business with this car?

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:55.790
I see, you're the previous owner of that FC, right?

00:21:55.790 --> 00:22:00.990
Yes, to be precise, this was the first
car the tuning shop, Zero, completed.

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:03.610
But, why is it so?

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:08.120
Of course, it was so worn down, so I fixed it up again.

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:10.630
It was covered in moss and rust.

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:11.870
You?

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:16.210
Well, yeah. So, what do you intend to do with that car?

00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:18.810
You came all the way from Tokyo to look for it.

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:22.340
I'd like you to sell it to me. I really want to drive it again.

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:25.880
Please, by all means!

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:29.090
I'll pay a suitable amount of money.

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:32.020
No, it's not a matter of money.

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:33.610
What do you mean...?

00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:37.610
This is a car I've taken really good care of. It's not a matter of money.

00:22:37.610 --> 00:22:39.570
Then, what can I offer?

00:22:41.180 --> 00:22:42.680
I want to ride in it, next to you.

00:22:43.330 --> 00:22:49.200
Then I will know what kind of feelings you have towards this car.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:03.260
<i>The driving style has not changed, it's just as it was before!</i>

00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:05.220
<i>I'm trembling so much I'm going numb!</i>

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:09.170
<i>Undoubtedly, this is my FC!</i>
